+> STOP. Captain's notes: non-binding. Captain writes, Captain trims. Anyone else: close this file now.
+
+# Captain Notes
+
+Binding behaviour lives in `.feature` specs and referenced `assets/**`. History lives in git. These notes carry only what the next cycle needs.
+
+## Current voyage
+
+Product: Vanilla-JS TodoMVC app, localStorage persistence, happy-dom verification tier.
+
+Scope: Full TodoMVC spec from `assets/app-spec.md`, base markup from `assets/app-template.index.html`.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- All 31 scenarios land in `@logic` tier: DOM-level happy-dom test, no external accounts.
+- 9 ordered watches in `watchbill.json`, grouped by feature seam (visibility, add, complete, delete, toggle-all, counter, clear-completed, edit, routing, persistence).
+- No `RIGGING.md` yet; greenfield bootstrap pending. Next role: Shipwright for fitting out, then QM on the watchbill.
+- The `assets/app-template.index.html` references `node_modules/todomvc-common/base.css` and `node_modules/todomvc-app-css/index.css`. These CSS dependencies need installing, or the paths adjusted to use `assets/base.css` if the base file is vendored.
+
+## Open items for next cycle
+
+1. Install `todomvc-common` and `todomvc-app-css` (or vendor the CSS from assets).
+2. Create `index.html`, `js/app.js`, `css/app.css` from the template.
+3. Dispatch Shipwright to fit out (derive `RIGGING.md`, `AGENTS.md`).
+4. Dispatch QM on the watchbill.
diff --git a/specs/todo-app.feature b/specs/todo-app.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7b9ca2d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/specs/todo-app.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,214 @@
+Feature: TodoMVC application
+  As a user managing tasks
+  I want a single-page todo app with create, edit, complete, filter, and delete
+  So that I can track work and see what remains
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded with no persisted todos
+
+  Rule: Section visibility
+
+    Scenario: Main section and footer hidden when no todos exist
+      Then the main section is not visible
+      And the footer is not visible
+
+    Scenario: Main section and footer visible after adding a todo
+      When the user adds a todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the main section is visible
+      And the footer is visible
+
+  Rule: Adding todos
+
+    Scenario: New todo appears in the list on Enter
+      When the user adds a todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the todo list contains 1 item
+      And the todo at position 1 has text "Buy milk" and is not completed
+
+    Scenario: Input is cleared after adding a todo
+      When the user adds a todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the new-todo input is empty
+
+    Scenario: Input is trimmed before creating a todo
+      When the user types "  Buy milk  " and presses Enter
+      Then the todo at position 1 has text "Buy milk" and is not completed
+
+    Scenario: Empty input is ignored
+      When the user types "   " and presses Enter
+      Then the todo list contains 0 items
+
+    Scenario: Input is focused on page load
+      Then the new-todo input is focused
+
+  Rule: Completing todos
+
+    Scenario: Clicking the checkbox marks a todo as completed
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      When the user toggles the todo at position 1
+      Then the todo at position 1 has text "Buy milk" and is completed
+
+    Scenario: Completed todo is not hidden from the list
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      When the user toggles the todo at position 1
+      Then the todo list contains 1 item
+
+  Rule: Deleting todos
+
+    Scenario: Clicking the destroy button removes a todo
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has added a todo "Walk dog"
+      When the user destroys the todo at position 1
+      Then the todo list contains 1 item
+      And the todo at position 1 has text "Walk dog" and is not completed
+
+    Scenario: Deleting the last todo hides main section and footer
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      When the user destroys the todo at position 1
+      Then the main section is not visible
+      And the footer is not visible
+
+  Rule: Mark all as complete
+
+    Scenario: Toggle-all checks all todos
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has added a todo "Walk dog"
+      When the user toggles mark-all-as-complete
+      Then the todo at position 1 has text "Buy milk" and is completed
+      And the todo at position 2 has text "Walk dog" and is completed
+
+    Scenario: Toggle-all reflects individual completion state
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has added a todo "Walk dog"
+      When the user toggles the todo at position 1
+      Then the mark-all-as-complete checkbox is not checked
+      When the user toggles the todo at position 2
+      Then the mark-all-as-complete checkbox is checked
+
+    Scenario: Toggle-all unchecks when any item is unchecked
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has added a todo "Walk dog"
+      When the user toggles mark-all-as-complete
+      Then the mark-all-as-complete checkbox is checked
+      When the user toggles the todo at position 1
+      Then the mark-all-as-complete checkbox is not checked
+
+  Rule: Counter
+
+    Scenario: Counter shows number of active items
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has added a todo "Walk dog"
+      Then the counter text is "2 items left"
+
+    Scenario: Counter updates when a todo is completed
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has added a todo "Walk dog"
+      When the user toggles the todo at position 1
+      Then the counter text is "1 item left"
+
+    Scenario: Counter uses singular for one item
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the counter text is "1 item left"
+
+    Scenario: Counter uses plural for zero items
+      Then the counter text is "0 items left"
+
+  Rule: Clear completed
+
+    Scenario: Clear-completed button removes completed todos
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has added a todo "Walk dog"
+      When the user toggles the todo at position 1
+      And the user clicks clear-completed
+      Then the todo list contains 1 item
+      And the todo at position 1 has text "Walk dog" and is not completed
+
+    Scenario: Clear-completed is hidden when no completed items exist
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the clear-completed button is not visible
+
+    Scenario: Clear-completed is visible when completed items exist
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      When the user toggles the todo at position 1
+      Then the clear-completed button is visible
+
+  Rule: Editing todos
+
+    Scenario: Double-click activates editing mode
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      When the user double-clicks the todo at position 1
+      Then the todo at position 1 is in editing mode
+      And the edit input at position 1 has value "Buy milk"
+
+    Scenario: Edit is saved on Enter
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      When the user double-clicks the todo at position 1
+      And the edit input at position 1 is changed to "Buy soy milk"
+      And the edit input at position 1 receives Enter
+      Then the todo at position 1 has text "Buy soy milk" and is not completed
+      And the todo at position 1 is not in editing mode
+
+    Scenario: Edit is saved on blur
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      When the user double-clicks the todo at position 1
+      And the edit input at position 1 is changed to "Buy soy milk"
+      And the edit input at position 1 receives blur
+      Then the todo at position 1 has text "Buy soy milk" and is not completed
+
+    Scenario: Empty edit removes the todo
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      When the user double-clicks the todo at position 1
+      And the edit input at position 1 is changed to ""
+      And the edit input at position 1 receives Enter
+      Then the todo list contains 0 items
+
+    Scenario: Escape discards changes
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      When the user double-clicks the todo at position 1
+      And the edit input at position 1 is changed to "Changed"
+      And the edit input at position 1 receives Escape
+      Then the todo at position 1 has text "Buy milk" and is not completed
+      And the todo at position 1 is not in editing mode
+
+  Rule: Routing
+
+    Scenario: All filter shows all todos by default
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has added a todo "Walk dog"
+      When the user toggles the todo at position 1
+      Then the filter "All" is selected
+      And the todo list contains 2 items
+
+    Scenario: Active filter hides completed todos
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has added a todo "Walk dog"
+      When the user toggles the todo at position 1
+      And the user navigates to "#/active"
+      Then the filter "Active" is selected
+      And the todo list contains 1 item
+      And the todo at position 1 has text "Walk dog" and is not completed
+
+    Scenario: Completed filter shows only completed todos
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has added a todo "Walk dog"
+      When the user toggles the todo at position 1
+      And the user navigates to "#/completed"
+      Then the filter "Completed" is selected
+      And the todo list contains 1 item
+      And the todo at position 1 has text "Buy milk" and is completed
+
+    Scenario: Completed todo disappears from active filter when toggled
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has added a todo "Walk dog"
+      When the user navigates to "#/active"
+      And the user toggles the todo at position 1
+      Then the todo list contains 1 item
+
+  Rule: Persistence
+
+    Scenario: Todos survive page reload
+      When the user adds a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user adds a todo "Walk dog"
+      And the user toggles the todo at position 1
+      And the app is reloaded
+      Then the todo list contains 2 items
+      And the todo at position 1 has text "Buy milk" and is completed
+      And the todo at position 2 has text "Walk dog" and is not completed
